  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2020-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Completing the square gives \\(x^{2020} + (y - 1)^2 = 1.\\) Both terms are nonnegative, so \\(x^{2020} \\le 1,\\) forcing \\(x \\in \\{-1, 0, 1\\}.\\)\n\nIf \\(x = 0,\\) then \\((y - 1)^2 = 1,\\) giving \\(y = 0\\) or \\(y = 2.\\) If \\(x = \\pm 1,\\) then \\(x^{2020} = 1,\\) so \\((y - 1)^2 = 0\\) and \\(y = 1.\\) The solutions are \\((0, 0), (0, 2), (1, 1),\\) and \\((-1, 1)\\) — four in all.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Complete the square in \\(y:\\) \\(x^{2020} + (y - 1)^2 = 1\\)",
        "Since \\(x^{2020} \\ge 0\\) and \\((y - 1)^2 \\ge 0,\\) only \\(x \\in \\{-1, 0, 1\\}\\) can work"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
